WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.863 --> 00:00:03.301
Line 3 in hall B needs more power.

2
00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:06.047
It comes from the electricity grid.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.367
Power is how fast you use energy.

4
00:00:10.036 --> 00:00:12.079
The grid is built for the highest power.

5
00:00:13.081 --> 00:00:14.648
Four topics follow the power.

6
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.810
First what flows and along which path.

7
00:00:18.892 --> 00:00:21.272
Then who runs it and why the grid is full.

8
00:00:22.574 --> 00:00:25.442
The first topic is Power, load and voltage.

9
00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:28.879
Voltage is the pressure and current is the flow.

10
00:00:29.861 --> 00:00:33.622
The grid must carry the highest power at one moment, the peak.

11
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.241
When line 3 starts up that is such a peak.

12
00:00:38.251 --> 00:00:40.852
The cable to hall B must handle that peak.

13
00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:45.154
For load you state the capacity of the cable in kVA.

14
00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:49.035
The second topic is The grid from high to low.

15
00:00:49.738 --> 00:00:51.700
At high voltage little is lost.

16
00:00:52.811 --> 00:00:56.631
Only close to the user do transformers step the voltage down.

17
00:00:57.647 --> 00:01:01.386
At the main fuse you read how much current the connection can take.

18
00:01:02.693 --> 00:01:05.607
The third topic is Roles, rules and money.

19
00:01:06.285 --> 00:01:09.118
The grid operator lays the cable to your connection.

20
00:01:10.093 --> 00:01:11.753
TenneT runs the highest grid.

21
00:01:12.652 --> 00:01:16.031
The supplier sells the energy and you choose it yourself.

22
00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.807
There is one grid per area.

23
00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:22.448
So a regulator sets the rules and the tariffs.

24
00:01:23.431 --> 00:01:27.436
For the rules you look up in the electricity system code how to connect.

25
00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:32.166
The fourth topic is Congestion and the energy transition.

26
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.807
In this region the grid is full.

27
00:01:35.746 --> 00:01:38.230
Whoever asks for more power joins the queue.

28
00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:42.577
Building a new substation often takes 5 to 10 years.

29
00:01:43.598 --> 00:01:47.557
You check the capacity map and sign a flexible contract if needed.

30
00:01:48.598 --> 00:01:52.371
Congestion usually lasts only a few hundred hours a year.

31
00:01:53.065 --> 00:01:56.827
So line 3 moves out of those hours and still gets power.

32
00:01:57.626 --> 00:01:59.472
Then the installer connects it.

33
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:01.622
The whole map.

34
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.452
The electricity grid is the first station of Energy and the grid.

35
00:02:07.487 --> 00:02:09.217
Every topic has four levels.

36
00:02:10.225 --> 00:02:14.880
Start with Volts, amps, watts and kWh at Basics level.

37
00:02:15.618 --> 00:02:18.729
That lesson shows why the grid runs on kilowatts.

38
00:02:19.751 --> 00:02:23.594
At Working knowledge level come simultaneity, the route to the socket,

39
00:02:23.838 --> 00:02:24.987
laws and the queue.

40
00:02:25.975 --> 00:02:28.854
At Advanced level come voltage along the cable,

41
00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:31.931
frequency, tariffs and what you can do yourself.

42
00:02:32.949 --> 00:02:36.885
At Expert level it is about metering data, the offshore grid,

43
00:02:37.082 --> 00:02:39.567
how operators earn money and the transition.

44
00:02:40.598 --> 00:02:44.778
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
